  "description": "Federal Express's colors from before the 1994 FedEx rebrand, repainted on a 777F. Fuselage: purple over the upper half from the nose to the fin, white below; a red-orange stripe along the side under the purple (a thin white line between them) that sweeps up behind the wing onto the fin. Fin: purple at the leading edge and tip, the stripe running up it parallel to the leading edge and turning aft under the tip, white behind it. Titles: 'FEDERAL' in white on the purple and 'EXPRESS' in red-orange under it on the white, both heavy extended capitals, ahead of the wing. Engines bare metal.",
