  "notes": "Measured on N884FD's left side at Beijing, 2026-10-30 (side-on, warm evening light: the colors are judged, not sampled). The stripe's long run is drawn straight in meters on the 777F (tools/edge_straightness.py straight_edge, fitted to four probes; it rises about 0.6 m nose to tail on the photo, kept). A thin white line separates the purple from the stripe; it's the base showing between them. The right side and the belly from below aren't measured; the second photo shows a white belly. The fin is taken as mirrored (as the paint sweeps) without a right-side photo. When it was painted isn't found: still in FedEx colors at Taipei 2026-01-11, in these by 2026-10-30. It recalls the original Federal Express scheme (purple, white and red-orange, 1973-1994); FedEx's own announcement wasn't found."
